antumcomputingreport.com/scorecards/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Scorecards</a><ul><li><a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/gate-level-software-platforms/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Gate Level Software Platforms</a><ul><li><a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/gate-level-quantum-software-platforms/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">IBM Qiskit, Rigetti Forest, Microsoft QDK, Project Q</a></li><li><a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/review-of-the-cirq-quantum-software-framework/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Review of the Cirq Quantum Software Framework</a></li></ul></li><li><a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/qubit-implementation-dashboard/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Qubit Implementation Dashboard</a></li><li><a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/qubit-count/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Qubit Count</a></li><li><a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/qubit-quality/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Qubit Quality</a></li><li><a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/qubit-technology/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Qubit Technology</a></li><li><a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/software-partners/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Software/Startup Partners</a></li><li><a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/cloud-platform-hardware-partners/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Cloud Platform Hardware Partners</a></li></ul></li><li><a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/podcasts/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Podcasts &amp; Interviews</a></li><li><a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/about/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">About</a><ul><li><a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/about/qcr-alerts-signup-form/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">QCR Alerts Sign-Up Form</a></li><li><a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/about/advertising-inquiries/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Advertising Inquiries</a></li><li><a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/about/qcr-in-the-news/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">QCR in the News</a></li><li><a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/about/contact-information/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Contact</a></li><li><a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/about/privacy-policy/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Privacy Policy</a></li></ul></li><li><a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/register/your-membership/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Membership</a></li></ul>\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFlorida International University Contracts IonQ for On-Premises Superion 256 Trapped-Ion Quantum Computer\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n<figure><a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/image-302.png\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/image-302-1024x701.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"1024\" height=\"701\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Trapped-ion quantum hardware manufacturer <a href=\"https://ionq.com/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">IonQ, Inc.</a> (NYSE: IONQ) has executed a commercial procurement agreement with <a href=\"https://www.fiu.edu/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Florida International University (FIU)</a> to supply and install an on-premises <a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/ionq-debuts-sixth-generation-superion-qpu-architecture-featuring-on-chip-electronic-control-and-cmos-integration/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">IonQ Superion</a> quantum computer. The contract establishes FIU as IonQ’s flagship academic partner in Florida, marking the first on-site installation of a 256-qubit trapped-ion system in the state.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The sixth-generation IonQ Superion architecture features 256 physical trapped-ion qubits engineered for high-density, reconfigurable all-to-all connectivity. Scheduled for installation in late 2027 following the completion of FIU’s dedicated campus data center facility, the system will provide direct physical compute access for FIU’s 1,200 faculty members, 56,000 students, and regional commercial partners across South Florida. Research workloads on the Miami campus will focus on material science, artificial intelligence, logistics optimization, cybersecurity, health sciences, and power grid management.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p>The agreement leverages FIU’s R1 research designation and its active briefing center in Washington, D.C., to align on-site quantum computing capabilities with federal research initiatives in sensing, cryptography, and national defense. The on-premises hardware deployment complements IonQ’s global cloud availability while strengthening regional quantum technology supply chains and workforce development programs across the Southeastern United States.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Review the official corporate press release via IonQ Investor Relations <a href=\"https://investors.ionq.com/news/news-details/2026/IonQs-Superion-256-Platform-Selected-by-Florida-International-University-for-Flagship-Deployment/default.aspx\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>September 24, 2026</p>\n\n                    <a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/florida-international-university-contracts-ionq-for-on-premises-superion-256-trapped-ion-quantum-computer/#\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">\n                    <img src=\"https://cdn.printfriendly.com/buttons/printfriendly-pdf-button.png\" alt=\"Print Friendly, PDF &amp; Email\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" />\n                    </a>\n                \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/author/mohamed-abdel-kareem/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Mohamed Abdel-Kareem</a>2026-09-24T22:29:24-07:00\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t\n\t<p>This site uses Akismet to reduce spam. <a href=\"https://akismet.com/privacy/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Learn how your comment data is processed.</a></p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t  \n\t\t\t\t  \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t \n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/florida-international-university-contracts-ionq-for-on-premises-superion-256-trapped-ion-quantum-computer/#\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Page load link</a>\n\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t<a href=\"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/florida-international-university-contracts-ionq-for-on-premises-superion-256-trapped-ion-quantum-computer/#\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\tGo to Top\n\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
